    {
      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "07af97432556d6b3ee9f2c322145fa1b",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"massless-form-factor-triangle\">Massless form-factor triangle</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><a href=\"/\">Browse all notebooks</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"/?file=hep/ibp_bubble.py\">Unequal-mass bubble</a> \u00b7\n<a href=\"/?file=hep/ibp_differential_equations.py\">Differential equations</a></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Vertex form factors with two on-shell massless legs contain\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D_1=k^2||)</marimo-tex>, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D_2=(k-p)^2||)</marimo-tex>, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D_3=(k-p-q)^2||)</marimo-tex>, where\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(p^2=q^2=0||)</marimo-tex> and <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(s=2p\\cdot q\\ne0||)</marimo-tex>. Mass insertions and expansions raise\npropagator powers. RustRed reduces these integrals at symbolic dimension\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D||)</marimo-tex>, before the Laurent expansion at <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D=4-2\\epsilon||)</marimo-tex>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The ordinary triangle reduces to a bubble with a <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(1/(D-4)||)</marimo-tex> coefficient.\nIts double infrared pole is therefore retained even though the bubble has\nonly a single ultraviolet pole. Setting <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D=4||)</marimo-tex> during reduction would lose\nthis information.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
